# Force LF line endings for all text files, regardless of platform checkout settings.
#
# Without this, Windows runners (Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true) rewrite LF to
# CRLF on checkout. Swift's `String.split(separator: "\n")` treats "\r\n" as a single grapheme
# cluster, not two characters, so a CRLF-converted file collapses into one "line" when diffed by
# swift-snapshot-testing's line-based `.json` strategy — turning a byte-identical snapshot into a
# spurious full-file mismatch on Windows only.
* text=auto eol=lf
